# **Coming home, and holding W into the rig anyway.**
#
# The demo hub with the boat twenty metres west of it, bow on, and the player
# at the wheel. `extends`, not a copy: **two fields differ** — where the boat
# is and where the player is — and the movement script is the shipped
# `deeper_player.rhai`, driven by `loom sim --hold`.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# `rig_drive.loom` measures her in thirty metres of open water, where nothing
# is in the way and her trim stays inside four centimetres. Arriving is the
# other half of every journey and it is the half with a wall in it, and that
# half was in no gate at all. Traced here, `--hold move_z=1`, before
# `STALL_TICKS` existed:
#
#   tick  120   boat y  -0.001   player y  1.681    still making way
#   tick  300   boat y  -0.333   player y  1.194    bow on the rig
#   tick  900   boat y  -0.691   player y  0.899
#   tick 2400   boat y  -1.463   player y  0.111    forty seconds, still going
#   tick 3000                    player y -0.696    swimming
#
# That is ADR 0063's submarining, reached at a thrust the helm calls
# *deliberately short of the ceiling*, by holding one key against something
# solid: the bow cannot move, the contact pitches her, body-frame thrust
# follows the bow down, and the two feed each other.
#
# **The rider is not falling through the deck.** His separation from the hull's
# origin over that whole descent is 1.601, 1.527, 1.590, 1.573 — inside seven
# centimetres, and the aft cockpit actually *rises* as the bow buries. He is
# riding a boat that is sinking, which is one defect and not two, and the
# `if grounded { vy = velocity[1]; }` line in `deeper_player.rhai` is not
# implicated.
#
# **It matters because it is not recoverable the way the sea is.** Let go and
# she floats back up (y = 0.031 by tick 3600) — twenty metres from her berth,
# against a closed rail, and nothing in this scene lets a swimmer climb aboard.
# The rig has a slipway for the player and nothing for the boat.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT IT MEASURES — three runs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   # 1. hold W into the rig for forty seconds: she stays a boat, you stay on
#   #    her
#   loom sim assets/test/rig_bump.loom --ticks 2400 --hold move_z=1 \
#     --assert "Rig/Boat.y > -0.4" --assert "Rig/Player.y > 1.2"
#
#   # 2. and she is still there a minute later, not creeping through it
#   loom sim assets/test/rig_bump.loom --ticks 3600 --hold move_z=1 \
#     --assert "Rig/Boat.y > -0.4" --assert "Rig/Boat.x < -20.0" \
#     --assert "Rig/Player.y > 1.2"
#
#   # 3. the limiter is a stall detector and not a speed limit: from the same
#   #    start, in clear water astern, she makes way and keeps it
#   loom sim assets/test/rig_bump.loom --ticks 900 --hold move_z=-1 \
#     --assert "Rig/Boat.x < -48.0" --assert "Rig/Player.y > 1.2"
#
# **Run 3 is the control.** A limiter that simply closed the throttle whenever
# `move_z` was held would pass runs 1 and 2 and would have deleted the boat.
# Astern is also the escape from run 1's stall and is deliberately unclamped:
# your speed is zero at the moment you first press S, so a symmetric limiter
# would hold the throttle shut exactly when you need it.
#
# Measured with the limiter in: she noses on at tick 300 with a 0.33 m dip,
# recovers to y = +0.030 by tick 600 and holds it to tick 3600, and the player
# stands at y = 1.60 for the whole minute.
#
# The boat is at x = -34 on the berth's own heading, so her bow (hull +X, about
# 9.5 m out) meets the rig's west face at x = -12 after thirteen metres — long
# enough to be at full speed when she gets there. The player sits at boat-local
# (-7.00, -, -1.80), the middle of `HelmMat`, the same spot `rig_drive.loom`
# uses.

[scene]
format = 1
id = "3d81c7b2-64a5-4f19-8e07-b21d95fa6c30"

[[prefab]]
key = "demo"
id = "b2a43f8f-314a-4d92-b4aa-322411869fcd"
path = "../games/deeper_demo.loom"

[[node]]
name = "Rig"
extends = "demo"

[[node]]
name = "Boat"
parent = "Rig"
transform = { pos = [-34.0, 0.0, 0.0] }

[[node]]
name = "Player"
parent = "Rig"
transform = { pos = [-41.00, 1.62, -1.80] }
